From 7c0ab9f1c16f79bb913b259b12d56ddad540b2f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:09:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Use standard-ish `rdp://` scheme to support most RDP apps on the host
---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a301439e868b6fc73260e51aee7f6f9e476ee52a..6286bcae75dd8fd06239084a4dcab0a69724a31e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -29,6 +29,14 @@ Install the tools for the host setup:
 
     sudo dnf install waypipe virt-firmware pinentry-gnome3
 
+Install a client for `rdp://` links, such as Remmina:
+
+    flatpak install flathub org.remmina.Remmina
+
+Set the client as the default handler for `rdp://` links:
+
+    xdg-mime default org.remmina.Remmina.desktop x-scheme-handler/rdp
+
 Build the binary and install the pieces into your user directories:
 
     make install
@@ -149,8 +157,8 @@
 ## Flatpak
 
 The manifest sits at flatpak/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json. It builds
-virtiofsd, passt, swtpm, socat, waypipe, FreeRDP, the OVMF firmware pair, and
-Phial itself from source. Run `make flatpak`. Read
+waypipe, the OVMF firmware pair, and Phial itself from source. Run
+`make flatpak`. Read
 [flatpak/README.md](flatpak/README.md) for the module list and the
 permissions. QEMU runs on the host.
 
diff --git a/docs/DESIGN.md b/docs/DESIGN.md
index 549994a79f6c1dc5f75b6932ef2c2d5beac2e94e..0f43f44d4176f34b9569cb60f5b64ac8433f8235 100644
--- a/docs/DESIGN.md
+++ b/docs/DESIGN.md
@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@ - The pencil opens Machine Settings.
 - The menu carries Logs, Reprovision the Guest Agent, Restart, and Delete Machine.
 - Logs opens the log of the machine in the text editor: the console of the installer when it keeps one, else the service log of the machine.
 - The Serial Console and Remote Desktop dialogs state the user and the password with a copy control for each, because the guest asks for both at its login.
+- The Remote Desktop dialog carries the `rdp://` link of the machine. It opens the link in the default handler of the desktop.
+- The link uses `localhost`, which resolves to `::1` first. The forward listens on the IPv6 loopback only.
 - The Terminal dialog carries Unlock the SSH Agent, which loads the key of the user into the agent of the session and asks for the passphrase through pinentry.
 - Every command in the guest states a timeout, so a guest that stops answering states an error instead of holding the app.
 - The install provisions the machine: it boots the guest once, waits for the guest agent to answer, copies the units of the guest into it, and stops it again.
diff --git a/flatpak/README.md b/flatpak/README.md
index d0fd0719a24f097e0fe205474c1538cafae62f72..ef93e45b05a20575d08e1393339b19b7eb275603 100644
--- a/flatpak/README.md
+++ b/flatpak/README.md
@@ -33,9 +33,10 @@ repository.
 
 The machine tools stay on the host. The units that the host install writes run
 swtpm, virtiofsd, passt, socat, and QEMU on the host, and QEMU reads the OVMF
-pair from the host. The RDP client also runs on the host: the window starts
-xfreerdp through flatpak-spawn. A bundle copy of these tools cannot serve the
-host QEMU or the host client, because /app exists only inside the sandbox.
+pair from the host. The RDP client stays outside the bundle as well. The window
+opens an `rdp://` link, and the handler of the desktop starts the client. A
+bundle copy of these tools cannot serve the host QEMU or the host client,
+because /app exists only inside the sandbox.
 
 ## Permissions
 
@@ -50,8 +51,8 @@   keyring of the session.
 - `--talk-name=org.freedesktop.systemd1` starts and stops the user units that
   run the machine, the gate, and the tools.
 - `--talk-name=org.freedesktop.Flatpak` runs the tools of the host through
-  flatpak-spawn, because ssh-add, gpg, run0, xfreerdp, and pinentry live outside
-  the sandbox.
+  flatpak-spawn, because ssh-add, gpg, run0, and pinentry live outside the
+  sandbox.
 - `--filesystem=~/.config/phial`, `--filesystem=~/.local/share/phial`, and
   `--filesystem=xdg-run/phial` share the state of the host install.
 - `--filesystem=~/.ssh` reads the public keys that the session agent holds.
@@ -69,8 +70,9 @@
 - qemu-system-x86_64 and edk2-ovmf for the machine.
 - swtpm, virtiofsd, passt, and socat for the units.
 - ssh-agent from openssh, for the session agent.
-- ssh-add, ssh-keygen, ssh, gpg, and xfreerdp for the tools that flatpak-spawn
-  runs.
+- ssh-add, ssh-keygen, ssh, and gpg for the tools that flatpak-spawn runs.
+- Remmina, or another client for `rdp://` links, for the Remote Desktop
+  control.
 - pinentry-gnome3 and run0 for the gate and the root setup.
 - virt-fw-vars for the Secure Boot enrollment.
 
